 | `INFRX_RELEASE_SHA` / `INFRX_IMAGE` | unset | the commit `install.sh` deployed (its HEAD, `--release`) and the runtime image id it built (`sha256:<64 hex>`), written by preflight `apply` (MANIFEST, required in `pilot`); the gateway exposes them as `infrx_build_info{revision, image} 1` on its loopback-only `/metrics` from startup, never read from git or docker at runtime (E4B's served-build check). A `pilot` without either refuses to start (`pilot.build_info`), and a malformed one refuses in every mode (`validate_deployment`) |
 | `WORKER_HEALTH_PORT` | 8002 | I2B-R4 (W3 request 6): the loopback port of `python -m infrx.worker` (`/readyz`, `/livez`, `/metrics` with the same `infrx_build_info`); bound only after the pool, the bucket and `PROCESSING_CACHE_DIR` answered. Read by the runtime, never written by the installer (`preflight.NOT_SETTABLE`): install.sh's `wait_ready` and `60-verify-local.sh` probe 8002 |
 | `PREPARATION_CONCURRENCY` | 2 (§5's `PilotSettings` default, not restated) | PREP-WORKER: the number of runners `python -m infrx.worker` runs on `prepare_dispatch` candidates (its preparation pool, beside `WORKER_CONCURRENCY`'s inference pool), and M2's per-process materialization gate; still gates nothing at admission (R1: `MAX_PREPARING_JOBS` does). Settable through the installer (`preflight.TUNABLE`). Its drain bound is `PREPARATION_LEASE_TTL_S`: an attempt still running at a SIGTERM is released and its lapsed lease requeued by the next `recover` (R93) ⚠️ TO BE VERIFIED on the box (no measured preparation latency) |
+| `ROLLOUT_ROUTING` | off (`1`/`true`/`yes`/`on` turn it on; anything else reads as off) | R1 (WR-R1-1): routes every admission (the ingress's and `POST /v1/jobs`, both through `Relay.accept`) through the Lab rollout router over D9's release store: explicit R62 pins served as asked, stable account cohorts, canary subjects admitted on the candidate's pin, shadow duplicates provider-funded and suppressed (never admitted, held or settled). Off, the relay's own accept serves and the launched API is unchanged; on without a router (`rollouts`) the gateway refuses to start. Read by the runtime, never written by the installer (`preflight.NOT_SETTABLE`): enabling it hosted needs D9's store, the E4 regression rerun (wave-5 plan rule 5) and P-12 |
 
 The four `DATABASE_POOL_*` names spell the prefix in full; `11 §F2R` item 7 wrote them as `DATABASE_POOL_MIN_SIZE/MAX_SIZE/CONNECT_TIMEOUT_S/STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS`, which this reads as one shared prefix rather than four different ones. The G1/Q1 constants are **not yet reads of these settings**: `validate.py`, `intake.py` and `scheduling/memory.py` belong to other tracks, so the wiring is an integration request, and `tests/contracts/test_config_and_imports.py::test_the_g1_and_q1_constants_match_the_deployment_defaults` pins the constants against these defaults so the two cannot drift while it is open.
 
